@copilot Fix the Temurin Renovate rule in this PR directly on its existing same-repository head branch `copilot/main-ff958ec8-22c0-42ac-97b4-5c49ce091c3b`. Keep that branch; if GitHub assigns a follow-up branch, keep the platform-assigned branch. Do not start further tasks or request any additional PRs.

Address both verified review findings and the Java 27 gap in one coding attempt. In `.github/renovate.json5`, Renovate's regex parser only appends `revision` if the `build` group is present, so the current expression compares `21.0.13_9-jdk` and `21.0.13_10-jdk` as equal; preserve the underscore build number for ordinary and security releases, and verify ordering across an ordinary build increment, a new security release, and the next ordinary patch. The existing Linux `27_35-jdk` and Windows `27_35-jdk-windowsservercore-ltsc2022` pins select the inherited rule, which rejects `27.0.1.1_4` tags even after permitting 27. Make the current 27 pins eligible for the matching patched release without editing either pin. Preserve major, OS/variant and JDK/JRE boundaries, and leave rolling tags and intentional historical fixtures alone. No manual image tags/digests, no Jib discovery changes, and no global Java policy changes.

Renovate resolves the `maintenance/v2.x` configuration's presets before merging it over main, so its Java LTS preset can supersede both the versioning and allowlist. Check effective config precedence, not just JSON syntax. Preserve maintenance branch-specific dependency compatibility rules. If the correct fix cannot take effect from main alone, identify the exact backport needed on the maintenance branch in your coding report; do not open it or modify unrelated configuration. Validate against representative tag pairs using real Renovate versioning/lookup behavior where feasible, and report which checks ran. Keep the diff narrow.

